    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0248" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.24/107a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the Polish
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-19T23:00:00-04:00">June 19, 1941—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2194. From Hopkins.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d243-f1"/> Poland included under
                        lend-lease.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d243-f2"/> We are now trying to get
                    equipment required for training purposes in Canada. Please advise Sikorski and
                    give him my warm regards.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="75" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p>Harry L. Hopkins, head of the Lend-Lease program.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d243-f2" n="76" xml:id="d243-f2-content">
                <p>President Roosevelt announced on September 4, 1941, that he had authorized the
                    transfer of various defense articles to the Government of Poland under the
                    Lend-Lease Act, and declared that the resistance of Polish forces was “vital to
                    the defense of the United States.” For text of announcement, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, September 6, 1941, p. 181. A master
                    lend-lease agreement was concluded with Poland on July 1, 1942; for text, see
                    Department of State Executive Agreement Series No. 257, or 56 Stat. 1542.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
